@startuml instance-lock-sequence
!pragma teoz true
skinparam defaultFontName "Noto Sans"
skinparam defaultFontSize 12
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam sequenceMessageAlign left
title The instance lock: one F1R3Gaze at a time writes a profile

box "F1R3Gaze (first process)" #F4F8FC
  participant "start-up\n(main.rs)" as Main #DDEBF7
  participant "InstanceLock::acquire\n(profile/lock.rs)" as Lock #DDEBF7
end box
box "Operating system" #F5FAF2
  participant "kernel:\nflock / LockFileEx" as Kernel #E2EFDA
  participant "<data>/instance.lock\n(the anchor)" as Anchor #FCE4D6
  participant "<runtime>/instance.lock" as Runtime #FCE4D6
end box
box "F1R3Gaze (second process)" #F4F8FC
  participant "start-up" as Second #DDEBF7
end box

Main -> Lock : acquire(layout, Mode::Window, now)
Lock -> Kernel : create <data>/ (0700) and open the anchor\n(O_CREAT, 0600)
Kernel -> Anchor : the file exists from now on
Lock -> Kernel : try_lock(anchor)
Kernel --> Lock : locked
Lock -> Kernel : create <runtime>/ (0700), open the runtime lock (0600)
Lock -> Kernel : try_lock(runtime)
Kernel --> Lock : locked
Lock -> Runtime : Linux: chmod 01600\n(the sticky bit keeps XDG cleaners away)
Lock -> Anchor : write pid, mode, start time, data root
Lock -> Runtime : write the same lines
Lock -> Lock : replace_unsynced instance.pid beside each lock:\nWindows forbids reading a locked file; not synced,\nsince a crash ends the hold it records
Lock --> Main : InstanceLock (held until the process ends)

== A second F1R3Gaze starts ==
Second -> Kernel : open the anchor, try_lock
Kernel --> Second : WouldBlock
Second -> Anchor : read instance.pid beside it
Second -> Second : LockError::Held: "another F1R3Gaze is using this\nprofile: process 4242 (window, since 2026-10-05T18:21:02Z)"
note over Second #FFF2CC
  The window, --headless and wallet commands that
  write exit with status 1. Commands that only read
  go on with the profile read-only.
end note

== The first process ends, however it ends ==
Main -> Kernel : exit, crash or kill: the files close
Kernel -> Kernel : both locks released by the kernel\n(runtime first on a clean exit)
note over Kernel #FCE4D6
  No stale lock: the next start takes both.
end note

legend right
  |= Colour |= Meaning |
  |<#DDEBF7> | F1R3Gaze code |
  |<#E2EFDA> | operating system |
  |<#FFF2CC> | what the user sees |
  |<#FCE4D6> | lock files, and what holds after a crash |
endlegend
@enduml
